    <header class="hero">
      <div class="hero-grid">
        <div>
          <div class="hero-tag">RURAL HERITAGE WITHOUT BORDERS</div>
          <h1 class="title">Do young people still feel <em>ownership</em> of their own village's heritage?</h1>
          <p class="hero-sub">
            Before a single workshop was designed, Asociația Vechea Bucovină asked. Between May
            and August 2026 the Romanian NGO ran a survey through its own Rural Heritage Data Hub,
            reaching young people in rural and small-town communities across six partner
            countries. What came back shaped every part of this project.
          </p>
        </div>
        <div class="specimen">
          <div class="stamp-num">294</div>
          <div class="stamp-lbl">Responses on file</div>
          <div class="stamp-row">
            <div><div class="n">6</div><div class="l">COUNTRIES</div></div>
            <div><div class="n">4.3</div><div class="l">CONFIDENCE /10</div></div>
            <div><div class="n">'26</div><div class="l">FIELD YEAR</div></div>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>

      <div class="ledger">
        <div class="cell"><div class="num">294</div><div class="lbl">forms completed during the research window</div></div>
        <div class="cell"><div class="num">6</div><div class="lbl">partner countries surveyed</div></div>
        <div class="cell"><div class="num">May–Aug</div><div class="lbl">the survey ran May through August 2026</div></div>
        <div class="cell"><div class="num">4.3/10</div><div class="lbl">avg. confidence heritage can become a real resource</div></div>
      </div>
    </header>

    <div class="field-row" id="context">
    
      <div>
        <div class="field-eyebrow">Why we asked</div>
        <h2>The gap between a living tradition and a museum piece</h2>
        <p class="desc">Some background on the pattern this survey was built to test.</p>
        <div class="tag-card context-card">
          <p>
            Digital and economic change has hit rural communities across Europe hard, and one of
            the clearest signs is the slow erosion of living identity paired with a steady outflow
            of young people. Traditional crafts, oral folklore and local customs are increasingly
            treated by young people as relics for a museum wall rather than something they could
            actually use to build a life at home.
          </p>
          <p>
            That cultural distance is made worse by a real lack of local opportunity, which pushes
            young people toward big cities and quietly wears down the ties between generations
            that used to hold rural communities together. <strong>UNESCO</strong> has pointed out
            that connecting young people to intangible cultural heritage through hands-on,
            non-formal learning is one of the more effective ways to protect local identity and
            support sustainable community development. <strong>Eurostat</strong>'s demographic
            data backs this up from a different angle: the working-age and youth population in
            the EU's rural regions is shrinking by roughly 0.6 to 0.7 percent a year, with more
            than 160 regions facing acute depopulation.
          </p>
          <p>
            To see how that plays out in its own cross-border network, rather than assume,
            Asociația Vechea Bucovină asked young people directly. The findings below are what
            shaped "Rural Heritage Without Borders" from the ground up.
          </p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="field-row" id="methodology">
      <div>
        <div class="field-eyebrow">Methodology</div>
        <h2>How this data was collected</h2>
        <p class="desc">A quick note on who ran it, who answered, and when.</p>
        <div class="method-grid">
          <div class="tag-card">
            <h3>Who ran it, and when</h3>
            <p>
              The survey ran on the Rural Heritage Data Hub tool <strong style="color:var(--ink);">from May through August 2026</strong>,
              led by <strong style="color:var(--ink);">Asociația Vechea Bucovină</strong> (Romania)
              during the preparation stage of the "Rural Heritage Without Borders" youth exchange.
              Respondents were young people connected to rural or small-town communities, reached
              through the six partner organizations' local networks.
            </p>
            <div class="closed-badge"><span class="sq"></span> SURVEY CLOSED, RESULTS ARE FINAL</div>
          </div>
          <div class="tag-card">
            <h3>Where responses came from</h3>
            <p>294 forms came in from young people across six partner countries:</p>
            <div class="countrylist">
              <span>🇷🇴 Romania</span><span>🇺🇦 Ukraine</span><span>🇵🇱 Poland</span>
              <span>🇨🇿 Czechia</span><span>🇲🇩 Moldova</span><span>🇲🇰 North Macedonia</span>
            </div>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="field-row" id="partners">
      <div>
        <div class="field-eyebrow">Who ran this study</div>
        <h2>One lead organization, six countries of reach</h2>
        <p class="desc">Asociația Vechea Bucovină designed and coordinated the research; five partner organizations ran it locally.</p>
        <table class="org-table">
          <tr class="lead">
            <td class="flag">🇷🇴 Romania</td>
            <td class="name">Asociația Vechea Bucovină <span class="lead-mark">LEAD · RESEARCH OWNER</span></td>
            <td class="desc">Poiana Stampei, Suceava county. Designed the survey, hosts the Rural Heritage Data Hub and coordinates the whole project.</td>
          </tr>
          <tr>
            <td class="flag">🇺🇦 Ukraine</td>
            <td class="name">NGO "NFED"</td>
            <td class="desc">Works with internally displaced youth and social adaptation through cultural practice, active in Mykolaiv and the Lviv region.</td>
          </tr>
          <tr>
            <td class="flag">🇨🇿 Czechia</td>
            <td class="name">EUnity, z.s.</td>
            <td class="desc">Cultural management and rural revitalization specialists, active in the Zlín district and Brno.</td>
          </tr>
          <tr>
            <td class="flag">🇲🇰 N. Macedonia</td>
            <td class="name">Eko-Zhivot</td>
            <td class="desc">Environmental and non-formal education organization running its own Eco-Education Centre in Kavadarci.</td>
          </tr>
          <tr>
            <td class="flag">🇲🇩 Moldova</td>
            <td class="name">JEF Moldova</td>
            <td class="desc">Youth facilitation and local storytelling, working with district youth councils including Glodeni district.</td>
          </tr>
          <tr>
            <td class="flag">🇵🇱 Poland</td>
            <td class="name">Fundacja Arbuzy</td>
            <td class="desc">Civic engagement work with schools across the Łódź Voivodeship, based in Tomaszów Mazowiecki.</td>
          </tr>
        </table>
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="field-row" id="findings">
      <div>
        <div class="field-eyebrow">Headline findings</div>
        <h2>Four numbers that shaped this project</h2>
        <p class="desc">These are the figures the whole "Rural Heritage Without Borders" proposal is built around.</p>
        <div class="stat-strip">
          <div class="cell"><div class="big">71%</div><div class="lbl">say they have almost no practical knowledge of the traditional crafts or heritage of their own region</div></div>
          <div class="cell"><div class="big">64%</div><div class="lbl">have considered moving to a bigger city because of a sense of isolation at home</div></div>
          <div class="cell"><div class="big">82%</div><div class="lbl">feel that heritage currently sits locked away in formal institutions, out of everyday reach</div></div>
          <div class="cell"><div class="big">78%</div><div class="lbl">want to learn practical crafts and start their own local youth initiative, given the right framework</div></div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="field-row" id="network">
      <div>
        <div class="field-eyebrow">Where the responses came from</div>
        <h2>294 young people, one square per two people</h2>
        <p class="desc">Every square is two respondents. Color marks which of the six countries they answered from.</p>
        <div class="tag-card waffle-wrap">
          <div>
            <div class="waffle-grid" id="waffleGrid"></div>
            <div class="waffle-note">147 SQUARES · 2 RESPONDENTS EACH · 294 TOTAL</div>
          </div>
          <div class="waffle-legend" id="waffleLegend"></div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="field-row" id="audience">
      <div>
        <div class="field-eyebrow">Who answered</div>
        <h2>Age and everyday setting</h2>
        <p class="desc">A young, mostly rural group, which is exactly who the exchange is designed for.</p>
        <div class="grid-2">
          <div class="tag-card">
            <h3>Age group</h3>
            <div class="ribbon" id="ageRibbon"></div>
            <div class="ribbon-legend" id="ageLegend"></div>
          </div>
          <div class="tag-card">
            <h3>Where they live</h3>
            <div class="ribbon" id="placeRibbon"></div>
            <div class="ribbon-legend" id="placeLegend"></div>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="field-row" id="interests">
      <div>
        <div class="field-eyebrow">Craft interests</div>
        <h2>What they'd actually want to learn</h2>
        <p class="desc">Asked which living craft or heritage practice they'd most want hands-on training in.</p>
        <div class="grid-2">
          <div class="tag-card">
            <h3>Top craft or heritage interest</h3>
            <div class="petal-wrap">
              <svg id="petalSvg" viewBox="0 0 230 230"></svg>
              <div class="petal-legend" id="petalLegend"></div>
            </div>
          </div>
          <div class="tag-card">
            <h3 style="text-align:center;">Confidence heritage can become a real resource</h3>
            <div class="gauge-wrap">
              <svg id="arcSvg" viewBox="0 0 200 118"></svg>
              <div class="gauge-num">4.3<span>out of 10, on average</span></div>
            </div>
            <div class="col-hist">
              <div class="c"><span class="pct">22%</span><div class="bar" style="height:76%;"></div><span class="lbl">0-2</span></div>
              <div class="c"><span class="pct">29%</span><div class="bar" style="height:100%;"></div><span class="lbl">3-4</span></div>
              <div class="c"><span class="pct">26%</span><div class="bar" style="height:90%;"></div><span class="lbl">5-6</span></div>
              <div class="c"><span class="pct">17%</span><div class="bar" style="height:59%;"></div><span class="lbl">7-8</span></div>
              <div class="c"><span class="pct">6%</span><div class="bar" style="height:21%;"></div><span class="lbl">9-10</span></div>
            </div>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="field-row" id="barriers">
      <div>
        <div class="field-eyebrow">Biggest barrier</div>
        <h2>What's standing between them and their own heritage</h2>
        <p class="desc">One required answer per respondent, ranked by share of votes.</p>
        <div class="tag-card">
          <div class="barrier-cols">
            <div class="c"><div class="val">29%</div><div class="bar" style="height:100%;"></div><div class="lbl">No access to knowledge holders or artisans nearby</div></div>
            <div class="c"><div class="val">24%</div><div class="bar" style="height:83%;"></div><div class="lbl">No non-formal framework to learn through</div></div>
            <div class="c"><div class="val">19%</div><div class="bar" style="height:66%;"></div><div class="lbl">Lack of funding or basic tools</div></div>
            <div class="c"><div class="val">15%</div><div class="bar" style="height:52%;"></div><div class="lbl">Heritage feels irrelevant to peers</div></div>
            <div class="c"><div class="val">9%</div><div class="bar" style="height:31%;"></div><div class="lbl">No platform to showcase their work</div></div>
            <div class="c"><div class="val">4%</div><div class="bar" style="height:14%;"></div><div class="lbl">Other</div></div>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="field-row" id="table">
      <div>
        <div class="field-eyebrow">Country data</div>
        <h2>Summary table of results</h2>
        <p class="desc">Key figures broken down for each of the six partner countries.</p>
        <div class="tag-card" style="padding:6px 6px 18px; overflow-x:auto;">
          <table class="country-t">
            <thead>
              <tr>
                <th>Country</th><th>Responses</th><th>Little craft knowledge</th>
                <th>Considered leaving</th><th>Want to launch</th><th>Top craft interest</th>
              </tr>
            </thead>
            <tbody id="tableBody"></tbody>
          </table>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="field-row" id="survey" style="border-bottom:none;">
      <div>
        <div class="field-eyebrow">For the next project</div>
        <h2>This round is closed, but the next one is open</h2>
        <p class="desc">Asociația Vechea Bucovină is already shaping the follow-up study. Your answer feeds into that, not into the numbers above.</p>
        <div class="survey-shell">
          <div class="survey-note">
            <h3>Help shape what comes next</h3>
            <p>
              The findings on this page are locked in, they belong to the May to August 2026
              round. But Asociația Vechea Bucovină and its five partner organizations are already
              preparing the next study, and it starts with the same kind of honest answers.
            </p>
            <div class="reopen-badge"><span class="sq"></span> NOW COLLECTING ANSWERS FOR THE NEXT PROJECT</div>
          </div>
          <form class="survey-form" id="surveyForm">
            <div id="formFields">
              <div class="f-group">
                <label>Where are you from?</label>
                <select name="country">
                  <option>Romania</option><option>Ukraine</option><option>Poland</option>
                  <option>Czechia</option><option>Moldova</option><option>North Macedonia</option>
                  <option>Other</option>
                </select>
              </div>
              <div class="f-group">
                <label>Your age group</label>
                <select name="age">
                  <option>15 to 17</option><option>18 to 21</option>
                  <option>22 to 25</option><option>26 to 30</option><option>Other</option>
                </select>
              </div>
              <div class="f-group">
                <label>Do you feel you have practical knowledge of your region's traditional crafts or heritage?</label>
                <select name="knowledge">
                  <option>Yes, quite a lot</option><option>Some</option>
                  <option>Very little</option><option>None at all</option>
                </select>
              </div>
              <div class="f-group">
                <label>How confident are you that heritage could become a real resource for your community's future?</label>
                <div class="slider-row">
                  <input type="range" min="0" max="10" value="5" id="confSlider">
                  <div class="slider-val" id="confVal">5</div>
                  <div class="slider-ends"><span>Not confident at all</span><span>Very confident</span></div>
                </div>
              </div>
              <div class="f-group">
                <label>What's the biggest barrier stopping you from learning about your heritage or launching a related initiative?<span class="req">*</span></label>
                <select name="barrier" required>
                  <option value="" disabled selected>Pick one option</option>
                  <option>No access to knowledge holders or artisans nearby</option>
                  <option>No non-formal framework to learn through</option>
                  <option>Lack of funding or basic tools</option>
                  <option>Heritage feels irrelevant to peers</option>
                  <option>No platform to showcase my work</option>
                  <option>Other</option>
                </select>
              </div>
              <button type="submit" class="submit">Submit answer for the next project</button>
            </div>
            <div class="thankyou" id="thankYou">
              <div class="check">✓</div>
              <h4>Thanks, we've got it</h4>
              <p>Your answer has been logged for the next project under "Rural Heritage Without Borders." The results on this page stay as they are.</p>
            </div>
          </form>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>

    <div style="padding:44px 0;">
      <div class="cta-strip">
        <div>
          <h3>This is where "Rural Heritage Without Borders" starts</h3>
          <p>These numbers, collected by Asociația Vechea Bucovină, became the basis for a 7-day youth exchange in Bucovina, Romania, plus follow-up workshops reaching young people in all six partner countries.</p>
        </div>
        <a class="cta-btn" href="index.html">← Back to Youth Data Hub</a>
      </div>
    </div>

    <footer>
      <div class="fmono">RURAL HERITAGE WITHOUT BORDERS · ERASMUS+ YOUTH EXCHANGE</div>
      <p class="fnote">
        Research designed and coordinated by Asociația Vechea Bucovină (Romania) and carried out
        from May through August 2026 with young people connected to rural and small-town
        communities in Romania, Ukraine, Poland, Czechia, Moldova and North Macedonia, together
        with partners NGO "NFED", EUnity z.s., Eko-Zhivot, JEF Moldova and Fundacja Arbuzy. The
        figures shown here fed directly into the design of the youth exchange and its follow-up
        activities.
      </p>
    </footer>

  </div>
</div>

<script>
  const slider = document.getElementById('confSlider');
  const confVal = document.getElementById('confVal');
  slider.addEventListener('input', () => { confVal.textContent = slider.value; });

  document.getElementById('surveyForm').addEventListener('submit', function(e){
    e.preventDefault();
    document.getElementById('formFields').style.display = 'none';
    document.getElementById('thankYou').style.display = 'block';
  });

  const COLORS = {
    Romania:'#C1613D', Ukraine:'#3F5D42', Poland:'#CC9A3E',
    Czechia:'#6B3F5B', Moldova:'#4A5A66', "North Macedonia":'#A34E2F'
  };

  const rows = [
    ["Romania", 58, "74%", "61%", "83%", "Woodworking"],
    ["Ukraine", 54, "69%", "72%", "81%", "Textile & embroidery"],
    ["Poland", 48, "65%", "58%", "74%", "Ceramics & pottery"],
    ["Czechia", 45, "68%", "55%", "77%", "Culinary heritage"],
    ["Moldova", 47, "77%", "70%", "80%", "Textile & embroidery"],
    ["North Macedonia", 42, "73%", "66%", "76%", "Music & oral folklore"],
  ];
  const tbody = document.getElementById('tableBody');
  rows.forEach(r => {
    const tr = document.createElement('tr');
    tr.innerHTML = `<td>${r[0]}</td><td class="num">${r[1]}</td><td class="num">${r[2]}</td><td class="num">${r[3]}</td><td class="num">${r[4]}</td><td>${r[5]}</td>`;
    tbody.appendChild(tr);
  });

  const waffleData = [
    {name:"Romania", squares:29, count:58},
    {name:"Ukraine", squares:27, count:54},
    {name:"Poland", squares:24, count:48},
    {name:"Czechia", squares:23, count:45},
    {name:"Moldova", squares:23, count:47},
    {name:"North Macedonia", squares:21, count:42},
  ];
  const waffleGrid = document.getElementById('waffleGrid');
  waffleData.forEach(d => {
    for(let i=0;i<d.squares;i++){
      const sq = document.createElement('div');
      sq.className = 'sq';
      sq.style.background = COLORS[d.name];
      sq.title = d.name;
      waffleGrid.appendChild(sq);
    }
  });
  const waffleLegend = document.getElementById('waffleLegend');
  waffleData.forEach(d => {
    const pct = Math.round((d.count/294)*100);
    const row = document.createElement('div');
    row.className = 'lg';
    row.innerHTML = `<span class="sw" style="background:${COLORS[d.name]};"></span> ${d.name} <span class="val">${d.count} · ${pct}%</span>`;
    waffleLegend.appendChild(row);
  });

  const ageData = [
    {name:"15 to 17", pct:8, color:'#C1613D'},
    {name:"18 to 21", pct:34, color:'#3F5D42'},
    {name:"22 to 25", pct:37, color:'#CC9A3E'},
    {name:"26 to 30", pct:21, color:'#6B3F5B'},
  ];
  const ageRibbon = document.getElementById('ageRibbon');
  const ageLegend = document.getElementById('ageLegend');
  ageData.forEach(d => {
    const seg = document.createElement('div');
    seg.className = 'seg'; seg.style.width = d.pct + '%'; seg.style.background = d.color; seg.textContent = d.pct + '%';
    ageRibbon.appendChild(seg);
    const lg = document.createElement('div'); lg.className = 'lg';
    lg.innerHTML = `<span class="sw" style="background:${d.color};"></span> ${d.name}`;
    ageLegend.appendChild(lg);
  });

  const placeData = [
    {name:"Rural village", pct:42, color:'#3F5D42'},
    {name:"Small town", pct:33, color:'#CC9A3E'},
    {name:"Regional town near rural area", pct:25, color:'#4A5A66'},
  ];
  const placeRibbon = document.getElementById('placeRibbon');
  const placeLegend = document.getElementById('placeLegend');
  placeData.forEach(d => {
    const seg = document.createElement('div');
    seg.className = 'seg'; seg.style.width = d.pct + '%'; seg.style.background = d.color; seg.textContent = d.pct + '%';
    placeRibbon.appendChild(seg);
    const lg = document.createElement('div'); lg.className = 'lg';
    lg.innerHTML = `<span class="sw" style="background:${d.color};"></span> ${d.name}`;
    placeLegend.appendChild(lg);
  });

  const petalData = [
    {name:"Textile & embroidery", pct:26, color:'#C1613D'},
    {name:"Woodworking & carpentry", pct:22, color:'#3F5D42'},
    {name:"Ceramics & pottery", pct:17, color:'#CC9A3E'},
    {name:"Culinary heritage", pct:15, color:'#6B3F5B'},
    {name:"Music & oral folklore", pct:12, color:'#4A5A66'},
    {name:"Natural building & land craft", pct:8, color:'#A34E2F'},
  ];
  const petalSvg = document.getElementById('petalSvg');
  const pcx = 115, pcy = 115, maxLen = 88, minLen = 22;
  const maxPct = Math.max(...petalData.map(d=>d.pct));
  const ns = "http://www.w3.org/2000/svg";
  function el(tag, attrs){
    const e = document.createElementNS(ns, tag);
    for(const k in attrs) e.setAttribute(k, attrs[k]);
    return e;
  }
  petalSvg.appendChild(el('circle', {cx:pcx, cy:pcy, r:14, fill:'#F5EDDC', stroke:'#2B2118', 'stroke-width':1.4}));
  petalData.forEach((d,i) => {
    const angle = (Math.PI*2*i)/petalData.length - Math.PI/2;
    const len = minLen + (d.pct/maxPct) * (maxLen-minLen);
    const x2 = pcx + len*Math.cos(angle);
    const y2 = pcy + len*Math.sin(angle);
    petalSvg.appendChild(el('line', {x1:pcx, y1:pcy, x2, y2, stroke:d.color, 'stroke-width':14, 'stroke-linecap':'round', opacity:'0.9'}));
    const lx = pcx + (len+20)*Math.cos(angle);
    const ly = pcy + (len+20)*Math.sin(angle);
    const t = el('text', {x:lx, y:ly, 'text-anchor':'middle', 'font-family':'Courier Prime, monospace', 'font-size':'10', fill:'#2B2118', 'font-weight':'700'});
    t.textContent = d.pct + '%';
    petalSvg.appendChild(t);
  });
  const petalLegend = document.getElementById('petalLegend');
  petalData.forEach(d => {
    const row = document.createElement('div'); row.className = 'lg';
    row.innerHTML = `<span class="sw" style="background:${d.color};"></span> ${d.name} <span class="val">${d.pct}%</span>`;
    petalLegend.appendChild(row);
  });

  const arcSvg = document.getElementById('arcSvg');
  const acx = 100, acy = 100, ar = 80;
  const circumference = Math.PI * ar;
  const value = 0.43;
  arcSvg.appendChild(el('path', {d:`M ${acx-ar} ${acy} A ${ar} ${ar} 0 0 1 ${acx+ar} ${acy}`, fill:'none', stroke:'#E4D8B8', 'stroke-width':14, 'stroke-linecap':'round'}));
  arcSvg.appendChild(el('path', {d:`M ${acx-ar} ${acy} A ${ar} ${ar} 0 0 1 ${acx+ar} ${acy}`, fill:'none', stroke:'#C1613D', 'stroke-width':14, 'stroke-linecap':'round', 'stroke-dasharray': `${circumference*value} ${circumference}`}));
  const t0 = el('text', {x:acx-ar+2, y:acy+18, 'font-family':'Courier Prime, monospace', 'font-size':'9', fill:'#786A52'}); t0.textContent='0'; arcSvg.appendChild(t0);
  const t10 = el('text', {x:acx+ar-10, y:acy+18, 'font-family':'Courier Prime, monospace', 'font-size':'9', fill:'#786A52'}); t10.textContent='10'; arcSvg.appendChild(t10);
</script>

</body>
</html>